From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: return an errno from a failed configuration or
 upload

aicwf_usb_probe() reaches system_config() and aicfw_download_fw() with ret
still 0 from aicwf_bus_start(). Both failure branches jump to
out_free_bus without setting it, so the probe frees usb_dev and returns 0
("failed with errno 0"). The driver core counts the interface as bound,
no other probe runs, and the radio stays down with no errno in the log.

The two reboot exits (system_reboot(), rwnx_send_reboot()) return 0
through the same label on purpose, because the part re-enumerates and a
new probe follows.

Store the result of system_config() in ret, with -1 (unknown chip)
mapped to -EIO. Set -EIO when aicfw_download_fw() fails, since its
failure branches return a bare -1. The stop-race stimulus, which takes
this exit, also sets -EIO. The reboot exits are not changed.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
index 8a2f07f..ba4510d 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -1978,6 +1978,7 @@ static int aicwf_usb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf, const struct usb_device_i
         rx_loader_inject_stop_race--;
         stop_race_pending = true;
         usb_err("stop race stimulus: error path after the bus start\n");
+        ret = -EIO;
         goto out_free_bus;
     }
 
@@ -1996,11 +1997,21 @@ static int aicwf_usb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf, const struct usb_device_i
 		goto out_free_bus;
 	}
 
-    if (system_config(usb_dev)) {
+    /* A failed configuration or upload leaves the part on the bus at its
+     * loader id, and no re-enumeration follows, unlike the two reboot
+     * exits above. Return an errno, so the driver core does not keep the
+     * interface bound to a probe that has freed everything. The upload
+     * returns a bare -1 (= -EPERM); say -EIO.
+     */
+    ret = system_config(usb_dev);
+    if (ret) {
+        if (ret == -1)
+            ret = -EIO;
         goto out_free_bus;
     }
 
-    if (aicfw_download_fw(usb_dev)){
+    if (aicfw_download_fw(usb_dev)) {
+        ret = -EIO;
         goto out_free_bus;
     }
     
